  "interfaces": {
    "induction": "Every use retains the explicit alternating rank bound at degrees 12<=m<n, with complete actual proper primitive, anchored-imprimitive and small-boundary interfaces in the acquired closure.",
    "critical_singleton": "Actual endpoint singleton plus complementary orbit gives n=2r>=14 and the natural Alt(n-1) omission in rank failure.",
    "least_later_cut": "The global-pairs theorem supplies a unique colour j>=2; minimality supplies actual ambient pairs for 2..j-1. The singleton-prefix lemma identifies C=a^(G_<j), proves suffix fixation, and puts all shared labels before j.",
    "singleton_opposite": "An interior singleton is excluded by its separate theorem. A terminal singleton invokes the reversed critical reduction and the exact paired-interior two-singleton theorem.",
    "unshared": "Connected string intervals and the two actual omission orbits give supported transitive prefix and suffix. No assumed transitivity of a projected factor enters.",
    "shared": "Reverse the full string with i=r-1-j and h=r-1-g. The preceding reversed group is original G_>j and fixes C; the tail is actual supported G_<g. All transitive-tail orientation hypotheses are paid.",
    "small_prefix": "The g=3 hand proof and the exhaustive uniform orbit budget for g>=4 exclude all intransitive prefixes. The separate finite fourth-prefix certificate is not a premise.",
    "maximal_crossing": "The retained full proof produces its singleton alternative at a later actual unique crossing j=r-1, hence exactly two omission orbits. This stronger internal conclusion, not merely an arbitrary singleton orbit, supplies Theorem1.",
    "closure": "The complete acquired proof and required-program dependency closure of each bound manuscript remains retained; accepted computations are not rerun or remeasured."
  },
  "new_statements": [
    "The complete endpoint-singleton branch satisfies the rank bound.",
    "With all maximal omissions intransitive, any unique ambient crossing forces the rank bound."
  ],
  "new_computation": false,
  "pending_packets_used_as_premises": false,
  "contributions": "The source cut strategy and all previously disclosed acquired arguments retain attribution. This continuation assembles the complete uniform singleton exclusions and checks every actual cut, orientation, singleton and induction interface."
}
